while man of steel was a divisive film  many would agree that henry cavill made  for an excellent superman not only did  he look great in the famous costume he  also seemed to embody the character  perfectly as a result fans have begged  to see more of cavill as superman he's  popped up in other projects since like a  batman v superman at dawn of justice and  justice league but he's not had the  chance to lead another solo project yet  since man of steel came out in 2013  warner brothers has been silent  regarding whether we'll see caval suit  up as a last son of krypton ever again  even when superman appeared in the final  episode of peacemaker season 1 a  different actor slipped into caval's  iconic suits and his face was never  shown and when superman briefly appeared  in shazam cavill was nowhere in sight  either there's a good chance we'll never  see cavill as a man of steel ever again  but it's undeniable that the actor is  immensely talented in fact many fans  have been left wondering if caval might  jump ship to marvel some have even  speculated that he could appear as  captain britain at some point in the  future plus one artist has imagined what  the actor could look like as one of the  most iconic characters in all of marvel  comics and that's wolverine for years  hugh jackman was wolverine the x-men  franchise went through various  iterations but the one constant was that  you could always expect jackman to show  up and lay down the hurt now that disney  owns 20th century studios fans are  eagerly awaiting an announcement about  when we'll see a new wolverine actor  rise up and take the reins there's a lot  of talk about who could feasibly take on  such an iconic role and henry cavill's  name comes up from time to time  instagram artist roy ledger has even  taken it upon themselves to envision  what caval could theoretically look like  in the role and the result is pretty  epic whereas jackman's wolverine was  rough but reasonably put together  leger's version is positively feral  sporting the character's iconic  sideburns from the comics as well as an  incredible mask that jackman didn't wear  during his run it certainly seemed to  have won over fans as plenty of people  have commented voicing their support for  the artwork for instance one fan  enthused definitely the best fan art out  there ever since this rumor came out  tapping mr sheik  still others think caval would be better  suited for a different mutant with one  fan bluntly writing nope way too tall  and he's better for cyclops i think  regardless of his next role it's clear  that most fans just want to see cavill  appear in another superhero property  sooner rather than later it may be a  while before we get another wolverine  introduced on film marvel studios has  yet to announce any upcoming x-men  projects despite having the rights to  the characters there's no doubt that  when wolverine's time comes it will be  one of the most hotly sought-after roles  in hollywood the question then becomes  is caval the right actor for the job  whether wolverine makes his debut in a  movie or a disney plus original series  there are plenty of qualities cavall  could bring to the part that make him an  ideal choice for starters he's an  incredible actor as evidenced by a  litany of eclectic paths in the likes of  the witcher and mission impossible  fallout plus cavill has experience  playing both good guys and bad guys so  he could embody both the heroic and  anti-heroic qualities of the character  be their hero clock  be their monument be their angel  be anything they need you to be  whether or not caval would be a good fit  for the role really depends on what  iteration of wolverine the mcu goes with  in the comics wolverine is supposed to  be around five foot two or five foot  three cavall stands at six foot one so  he's quite a bit taller than the  character granted hugh jackman was also  taller than wolverine's suggested height  but the mcu might want to make their  next adaptation more accurate to the  comics there's also the question of  whether or not caval would have time to  join the mcu in such a major capacity  with his prominent role in netflix's the  witcher only time will tell but there's  no doubt that the mcu would benefit  greatly from kabul's presence  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite superhero movies and tv  shows are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

